title: 'FRAME: reject duplicate view-function blocks and pallet indices'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Pallets now reject a second `#[pallet::view_functions]` block instead of silently keeping
    only the last block for metadata and runtime dispatch. Move all view-function methods into
    a single block, preserving any bounds required by those methods. The compiler points to
    the duplicate attribute.

    Repeated `#[runtime::pallet_index]` attributes on a pallet are now rejected, including when
    their values match. Keep exactly one attribute. Retain the last previously specified index
    to preserve the index used by the old macro and existing call/event encoding. No storage
    migration is required.
crates:
- name: frame-support-procedural
  bump: major
- name: frame-support
  bump: major
